Description: Fits multivariable fractional polynomial models with simultaneous
    selection of variables and functional forms for generalized linear models
    and Cox proportional hazards models. Key references are Royston and Altman
    (1994) <doi:10.2307/2986270> and Royston and Sauerbrei (2008,
    ISBN:978-0-470-02842-1). Extensions include approximate cumulative
    distribution transformations for sigmoid-shaped covariate effects, as
    described by Royston (2014) <doi:10.1177/1536867X1401400206> and Royston
    and Sauerbrei (2016) <doi:10.1177/1536867X1601600109>; spike-at-zero
    modeling for semi-continuous covariates using a two-stage selection
    procedure, following Becher et al. (2012) <doi:10.1002/bimj.201100263>;
    and fractional-polynomial interaction analyses between categorical grouping
    variables and continuous covariates, following Royston and Sauerbrei (2004)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.1815>, Royston and Sauerbrei (2013)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.5813>, and Royston and Sauerbrei (2014)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.6308>.
